  "body": "Found during the step-6 cutover (#5356): the via-service client in `crates/atlas-search/src/service.rs` builds its ureq agent with timeouts only — no proxy support. On hosts that reach the tailnet only through an HTTP CONNECT proxy (the sandbox: its tailnet tunnel proxy is the same egress host on port 3130), `ATLAS_SEARCH_URL=http://amd-6.raptor-pumpkinseed.ts.net:18760` is therefore unreachable directly: the connect times out and the CLI falls back to standalone. The fallback is loud and correct (verified live — warning on stderr, standalone results identical), so this is a capability gap, not a correctness bug.\n\nInterim state (working, shipped in the cutover): the sandbox's `atlas-search` wrapper asks the shared laptop-ssh control connection to forward loopback:18760 to the laptop and points `ATLAS_SEARCH_URL` at `http://127.0.0.1:18760`. That works (1.7s dedupe-class responses vs ~9.5 min for a standalone hybrid search over the proxy path), but it couples the CLI to the SSH tunnel.\n\nAsk: build the client agent with proxy-from-environment support (ureq 3: `Proxy::try_from_env` or equivalent, honoring HTTPS_PROXY/http_proxy + NO_PROXY), with a test that runs the client against a stub CONNECT proxy. Then the sandbox wrapper reduces to setting `ATLAS_SEARCH_VIA=service` + `ATLAS_SEARCH_URL`, and any other proxied host (codespaces, CI) gets the same path for free.\n\nNote the related asymmetry: the sandbox's egress proxy (port 3128) cannot complete TLS to `tailscale serve --https` endpoints, while the tailnet tunnel proxy (3130) reaches the fleet-standard `tailscale serve --tcp` forwards — the atlas serve mapping is therefore the tcp form. Proxy support in the client makes both forms usable from the sandbox.\n\nRefs #5356, epic #5350.\n",
